-    "documentation": "## Video Billboard\n\nA video playback system that displays videos or images on mesh surfaces using VideoTexture. Supports both external URLs and internal library assets with automatic fallback. Features proximity-based volume control, aspect ratio preservation, autoplay, looping, and rotation. Ideal for in-game screens, billboards, and environmental video elements.\n\n### Key Features\n- Video playback from URL or local library\n- Automatic fallback: tries alternative source on load failure\n- Aspect ratio preservation with cover/contain modes\n- Configurable video rotation (degrees)\n- Proximity-based volume control (distance-based fade)\n- Autoplay, loop, and muted options\n- Trigger-based play/stop control\n- Muted autoplay fallback for browser restrictions\n- VideoTexture with needsUpdate management\n- ScalingImageMaterial for proper aspect ratio fitting\n- Original material restoration on cleanup\n- WebGL texture optimization\n- Editor live preview with attribute updates\n\n### How It Works\n1. Attach to mesh object (or parent with mesh child)\n2. Configure video source:\n   - external_url: HTTP/HTTPS video URL\n   - internal_url: video from project library (enum)\n   - useLocalFile: prioritizes internal over external\n3. Set playback options:\n   - autoplay: starts immediately on load\n   - loop: repeats video endlessly\n   - muted: disables audio (helps with autoplay restrictions)\n   - volume: initial volume level (0.0-1.0)\n4. Configure display:\n   - aspect: geometry aspect ratio for fitting\n   - fit: 'cover' (fill) or 'contain' (letterbox)\n   - rotate: rotation angle in degrees (-360 to 360)\n5. Set proximity (optional):\n   - Distance threshold for proximity-based playback\n   - Volume fades based on distance to player\n6. On add:\n   - Stores original material for restoration\n   - Constructs video URL (prioritizes based on useLocalFile)\n   - Validates URL format (http/https protocols)\n   - Creates VideoSource instance\n7. VideoSource initialization:\n   - Creates HTMLVideoElement\n   - Loads video metadata (width, height)\n   - Creates THREE.VideoTexture from element\n8. Material creation:\n   - Calculates aspect ratio: video / geometry\n   - ScalingImageMaterial.createMaterial(texture, aspect, rotation)\n   - Replaces mesh material with video material\n9. Playback control:\n   - Autoplay: calls play() after video ready\n   - Trigger: responds to 'activate'/'deactivate' messages\n10. Update loop:\n    - Sets texture.needsUpdate = true when playing\n    - Proximity check: distance to player\n    - Volume calculation: distanceRatio * initialVolume\n    - Auto play/pause based on proximity threshold\n11. Fallback handling:\n    - On load error, tries alternative source\n    - Shows toast notifications for errors\n    - Attempts muted autoplay on NotAllowedError\n    - Falls back to gray placeholder material on total failure\n12. Cleanup/dispose:\n    - Pauses or stops video\n    - Restores original material\n    - Releases video resources (commented out - TODO)\n\n### Common Use Cases\n- In-game TV screens or monitors\n- Billboard advertisements in cities\n- Tutorial videos on surfaces\n- Security camera feeds\n- Cinematic screens in theaters\n- Video textures for environmental storytelling\n- Interactive kiosks with video content\n- Holographic displays\n- News screens in sci-fi environments\n- Music videos in nightclub scenes\n\n### When Not To Use\n- For skybox videos (use different approach)\n- When video should be 2D UI overlay (use HTML video element)\n- For 360-degree videos (needs a different material path)\n- When video needs transparency/alpha channel\n- For procedural video effects (use shaders)\n- When multiple videos should sync precisely\n- For streaming live video feeds (needs media server)\n- When video needs custom material effects\n- For VR stereo video (needs special format)\n- When video should be interactive/clickable (needs raycast)\n\n### Technical Details\n- VideoSource class: manages HTMLVideoElement and VideoTexture\n- Video loading: async createVideoSource() returns promise\n- Width/height: videoSource.getWidth()/getHeight() from video element\n- Aspect ratio: (videoWidth / videoHeight) vs (geometryAspect)\n- Fit modes: cover (imgAspect/geoAspect), contain (geoAspect/imgAspect)\n- Rotation: converted to radians (degrees * PI / 180)\n- ScalingImageMaterial: custom node material for aspect-aware scaling\n- Texture update: texture.needsUpdate = true on playing frames\n- Proximity distance: distanceTo(playerPosition) each frame\n- Distance ratio: max(0, min(1, 1 - distance / proximityDistance))\n- Volume calculation: distanceRatio * initialVolume\n- URL validation: new URL(string) with protocol check\n- Fallback logic: catch block tries opposite source (external->internal)\n- Toast notifications: showToast() for user feedback\n- Play restrictions: NotAllowedError triggers muted autoplay attempt\n- Browser autoplay policy: muted videos more likely to autoplay\n- Video element: injected into document.body\n- Renderer: passed to VideoSource for texture creation\n- Material replacement: mesh.material = videoMaterial\n- Original material: stored in originalMaterial property\n- Cleanup flag: wasPlayingBeforeDispose for editor attribute updates\n- State tracking: isPlaying boolean\n- Editor updates: full dispose and reinit on URL change\n- Partial update: only material recreation if URL unchanged\n- Trigger support: startOnTrigger flag + onEvent() handler\n- Throttle: MEDIUM priority, frustum/distance culling enabled\n- TODO: Proper video resource release (commented out)"
